{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pulls/117","id":4509837105,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSvcS2c8AAAABDM6nMQ","html_url":"https://github.com/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pull/117","diff_url":"https://github.com/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pull/117.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pull/117.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/issues/117","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pulls/117/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pulls/117/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/issues/117/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/statuses/b6a275d5ca3455b2d7de6dc3d23c50fa171c4235","number":117,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat: add restart-safe local-first inference runner","user":{"login":"pashamango","id":141678664,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHHYSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141678664?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango","html_url":"https://github.com/pashamango","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# FREE-INFERENCE-RUNNER-0001\n\nVerdict: `RUNNER_READY`\n\nThis slice is a loopback/local-first SQLite-WAL runner. Jobs are `queued -> completed`; an external job remains `queued` when its capability is `auth_required`, so missing Google authorization does not block local work. Completed jobs return the stored result and receipt on restart or duplicate processing, preventing duplicate semantic execution.\n\nPrivate or marker-sensitive input is local-only. Public synthetic input may use the narrow provider adapter. The adapter receives a request, not a reusable credential; the worker exposes only sanitized capability metadata. Paid mode is rejected and every job carries a free-only budget envelope.\n\nThe local adapter uses Ollama at `127.0.0.1:11434`, model `gemma4:latest`, with `stream:false` and `think:false`, the smallest proven configuration fix from predecessor findings. External activation is represented by `NoAuthExternal` and tested with `StubExternal`; no account, billing, network listener, or secret was changed. Exact live runtime/model latency is reported only when a live receipt is available; deterministic tests use `fake-local`/`stub-v1`.\n\nOperations submits with `Runner(db).submit(job_id, prompt, privacy)` and retrieves with `process(job_id)`. Receipts include task id, route, observed provider/model, latency, retries, exposed usage counters, and result SHA-256. `capability_card()` implements `worker-capability-card/v1` with task/privacy classes, lane availability, bounded capacity, and no private host fields.\n\nChecks: `python -m unittest discover -s tests -v` (4 tests). The restart/idempotency, private/public routing, no-auth queueing, budget guard, receipt hash, and sanitized capability-card cases pass. Smallest next step: separately authorize and implement one external adapter behind the existing capability boundary; no AUTH_REQUEST is made here.\n","labels":[],